              "rationale": "The <html> element in product.html has no lang attribute. Without one, screen readers have to guess the page language and may read it with the wrong voice or pronunciation. All the page text is English: \"Speckled mug, 350 ml\", \"Dishwasher safe\", \"Quantity\", \"Add to basket\". The £ price and the word \"basket\" suggest British English, so the patch sets lang=\"en-GB\". If the site targets English speakers in general rather than the UK, plain lang=\"en\" would also work. I searched the repo and no other file sets lang, so there is no existing convention to match. A reviewer should confirm the regional variant.",
